{
 "summary": "Fixed semver.diff misclassification when going from a prerelease to a release (e.g. 3.4.6-2 -> 3.5.2 returned 'patch', now 'minor'). The special case in functions/diff.js previously judged the level from absolute values on the release (highVersion.patch / highVersion.minor), so any prerelease with a nonzero patch was capped at 'patch' even when the minor had been bumped. It now keeps the documented 'X.0.0-pre is always major' shortcut and otherwise compares the two versions component by component (major -> minor -> patch), with an equal-components tail that classifies completing the prerelease's own line (0.1.0-1 -> 0.1.0 minor, 0.0.2-1 -> 0.0.2 patch, 1.0.0-1 -> 1.0.0 major). All 48 test files pass."
